# AI workflow (Porirua Locality monorepo)

## Repository layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `porirua_directory/` | Services directory MVP (data pipeline, static UI, tests) |
| `porirua_connections_map/` | Community Connections Map (Squarespace embed, sheet/CSV) |
| `docs/` | Requirements, architecture, runbook, phase specs, plans |

See root `AGENTS.md` and `docs/README.md` for indexes.

## Documentation (keep in sync)

When you change **behavior**, **data rules**, **deploy**, or **editor workflow**, update the matching doc in the **same change set** (same commit when the user asks to commit):

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| System / hosting / data flow | `docs/architecture/porirua-directory-architecture.md` |
| FSD filter, merge, schema, overrides | `docs/porirua-directory-phase1-spec.md` + `docs/fsd-porirua-filter-rationale.md` (geo rules & audit) |
| Rebuild, deploy, manual steps | `docs/MVP-RUNBOOK.md` |
| Product scope / budget / phases | `docs/porirua-services-directory-requirements.md` (+ changelog/version there) |
| App-specific usage | `porirua_directory/README.md` or `porirua_connections_map/README.md` |

Do not leave docs stale after code or pipeline changes.

## Commits

- **Only commit when the user explicitly asks.** If unclear, ask first.
- Follow the user’s git safety rules: no `--no-verify`, no secrets (`.env`, credentials), no force-push to main unless requested.
- Messages: **complete sentences**, focus on **why**; group logically related changes; include doc updates with related code.
- If a feature or large change was materially **agent-assisted**, note that in the commit body or PR description.

## Verification before “done”

- **Directory data/scripts:** `cd porirua_directory && npm test` (and `npm run build:data` when touching merge/import).
- **Directory E2E:** `npm run test:e2e` when UI or critical flows change.
- **Static UI:** no automated suite in map app — state what was checked manually (local serve, key filters/search).

Do not claim work is complete without running relevant checks and confirming output.

## Scope

- Minimal diffs; match existing style; no drive-by refactors.
- One concern per commit when the user asks for multiple commits; otherwise one logical commit is fine.
